  ('Honey-Cured Candied Bacon','Wild River IPA Series','Beer','The honey cure''s sweetness and the bacon''s fat are a classic foil for bold hop bitterness — the IPA''s resinous, dry finish cleanses the palate, while the crushed red pepper amplifies the beer''s citrus heat.',NULL,1),
  ('Japanese A5 Wagyu Ribeye (6 oz)','2022 Far Niente Post & Beam Cabernet Sauvignon','Red','The extraordinary fat content of Japanese A5 Wagyu softens the wine''s tannins beautifully, allowing the mocha and blackcurrant notes to shine against the beef''s buttery richness — a textbook luxury pairing.',NULL,1),
  ('Jumbo Asparagus','2021 Pascaul Clement Puligny Montrachet','White','The Meyer lemon in this dish is a direct echo of the wine''s citrus core, and the wine''s mineral, saline finish plays off the grassy bitterness of the asparagus for a clean, refreshing contrast.',NULL,3),
  ('Jumbo Asparagus','2022 Punta Crena Vermentino ''Vigneto Isasco''','White','Asparagus with olive oil and Meyer lemon is a classic Ligurian pantry combination, and the wine''s crushed-herb aromatics and green-almond bitterness align naturally with asparagus''s vegetal character, making this one of the most regionally intuitive pairings on the menu.',NULL,3),
  ('Jumbo Asparagus','2022 Savary Chablis ''Vaillons''','White','The Meyer lemon finish on the asparagus echoes the wine''s own citrus zest and bright acidity, while the vegetable''s subtle grassy bitterness finds a natural counterpart in the Chablis'' dried herb and mineral backbone.',NULL,3),
  ('Jumbo Asparagus','2023 Bruno Colin Bourgogne Chardonnay','White','Grassy, green-edged asparagus is a natural affinity for this style of Chardonnay, and the Meyer lemon dressing directly mirrors the wine''s citrus core, making both taste more vibrant.',NULL,3),
